we begin this morning with president  biden in poland and preparing to get a  first-hand look at the human toll of  russia's war against ukraine the united  nations estimates more than a thousand  civilians have been killed and at least  1600 others were wounded in the besieged  southern port city of mary opal this  includes 300 people in an attack on the  theater that was being used as a bomb  shelter and had the word children  written in big letters on the ground  outside this morning mr biden dropped in  on a meeting between secretary of state  lincoln  defense secretary austin and their  ukrainian counterparts on friday the  president thanked members of the 82nd  airborne who are part of nato's eastern  front poland has taken in a majority of  the nearly four million people who have  fled russia's invasion today mr biden  plans to meet with some of them nancy  cordes is traveling with the president  and begins our coverage in warsaw nancy  good morning  good morning to you jeff a somewhat  extraordinary meeting taking place here  in warsaw this morning president biden  at his hotel sitting down with the  ukrainian foreign minister the ukrainian  defense minister who left their country  overnight to travel here to warsaw about  130 miles from the border so that the  president could hear firsthand what they  need and how the u.s can help  real-time diplomacy between the leader  of the free world and leaders of a  war-torn nation  with 9 000 u.s troops now stationed in  poland president biden came to thank  them and prepare them for what could be  a prolonged mission on nato's eastern  flank  you're the finest fighting force in the  history of the world the 82nd airborne  is stationed in jeshaf poland providing  humanitarian aid in a town that has now  become a processing point for tens of  thousands of refugees the ukrainian  border is just 50 miles away they will  not let me understandably i guess it  cross the border and  take a look what's going on  in ukraine the russian strategy appears  to be shifting  pentagon officials say they see signs  that russia is bringing in more troops  from a russian occupied region of nearby  georgia  and they say the russian military is no  longer advancing towards kiev pentagon  press secretary john kirby why do you  think they're doing that well it's hard  to know it could be a negotiating tactic  maybe he wants to secure more ground  where he already has been fighting now  for eight years  so that he can gain leverage at the  negotiating table we're not sure  today on president biden's last day in  europe he is meeting with ukrainian  refugees he'll also deliver a speech for  hundreds here in warsaw and his aides  say he wants to not only show support  for poland and ukraine but also here in  eastern europe cast this conflict as a  broader battle between democracy and  autocracy jeff  nancy cordes thank you very much in  warsaw poland
 

